    "end": "Her dad was out fishing.",
    "caption": "Holly lives in that little house.\n\nFlicker: 410,000 people, a 22-hour day, one moon that's rarely needed, and a sea that lights up for every first kiss on the coast. Most nights it flickers a bit. Fishermen read it like a newspaper, and the harbour master keeps a chart. Matt walked Holly home along the front every Friday for a year. Every Friday, the sea stayed dark, and the whole town noticed.\n\nI stood on the pier for an hour to see it. The sea gave me one dim flicker, out of pity.\n\n(On Earth, some bays glow blue at night: a plankton called sea sparkle lights up whenever the water's disturbed. Nobody has to kiss anyone.)\n\nHow long did yours take to make a move?"
  },
  "first_comment": "Her dad caught nothing that night. He blames the light.",
